-- title:
--   Iwasawa evaluation of a truncated pairing of induced sections
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, let $\alpha$ be the homomorphism from the ideles $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ to $\mathbb{R}^\times$ induced by the distributive Haar character of the adele ring followed by $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}\to\mathbb{R}$, and assume $\alpha(t)>0$ for all $t$. Let $c\in[0,\infty]$ with $c\neq\infty$ satisfy the Iwasawa disintegration hypothesis: for all measurable $D,D'$ that are fundamental domains for the principal ideles (the image of $F^\times$) acting on $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ with idelic Haar measure, and every measurable $f\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to[0,\infty]$ invariant under left multiplication by $T(F)N(\mathbb{A}_F)$ (the subgroup generated by rational central and rational $\mathrm{diag}(t,1)$ elements together with the adelic unipotent subgroup), the lower integral of $f$ over representatives on the quotient, for the quotient Haar measure, equals $c\int_D\int_{D'}\int_{\mathbf{K}} f(z\cdot\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\cdot k)\,\lVert t\rVert^{-1}$, with $z$ central, $\mathbf{K}$ the adelic maximal compact subgroup with its Haar measure and $\lVert\cdot\rVert$ the idele norm. Fix such $D,D'$; let $\mu,\nu,\mu',\nu'$ be characters of the ideles into $\mathbb{C}^\times$ of absolute value $1$ that are trivial on principal ideles, $s,s'\in\mathbb{C}$, and let $\varphi,\varphi'$ be continuous functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ satisfying $\varphi(bg)=\eta_1(b_{11})\eta_2(b_{22})\varphi(g)$ for $b$ with $b_{21}=0$, where $\eta_1=\mu\,\alpha^{s+1/2}$, $\eta_2=\nu\,\alpha^{-(s+1/2)}$, and correspondingly for $\varphi'$ with $\mu',\nu',s'$. Let $a,b,R,R'\in\mathbb{R}$ with $a>0$. Then the function on the quotient given at a representative $g$ by $\mathbf 1_{[a,b]}(\lVert\det g\rVert)\,\mathbf 1_{(e^R,e^{R'}]}(\mathrm{ht}(g))\,\varphi(g)\overline{\varphi'(g)}$, with $\mathrm{ht}$ the adelic height, is integrable for the quotient measure, and its integral equals $c$ (as a real number, viewed in $\mathbb{C}$) times $\int_{\mathbf K}\varphi(k)\overline{\varphi'(k)}\,dk$ times $$\int_D\int_{D'}\eta_1(zt)\eta_2(z)\overline{\eta_1'(zt)\eta_2'(z)}\,\mathbf 1_{[a,b]}\!\left(\lVert z\rVert^2\lVert t\rVert\right)\mathbf 1_{(e^R,e^{R'}]}(\lVert t\rVert)\,\lVert t\rVert^{-1}.$$
--
--   This is the Iwasawa-coordinate evaluation of the inner product of two induced (principal series) sections, truncated by a slab condition on the norm of the determinant and by a shell condition on the adelic height, reducing the integral over $T(F)N(\mathbb{A}_F)\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ to a compact-group pairing times a double idelic integral. It feeds the Maass–Selberg type computations for truncated pseudo-Eisenstein pairings and the determination of the residue of the Weyl intertwining operator at the self-dual point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_integral_rationalTorusUnipotentQuotient_section_mul_conj_eq_mul_setIntegral_iwasawa.lean

